WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:03.610
We have to talk about something really important
today.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:09.460
And the reason that this is so important is
that we can't solve problems unless we understand

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.460
them.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.480
And over the last few days, has different
folks have weighed in on the violent Trump

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.710
insurrection that took place last week?

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:20.630
I've seen more and more commentaries that
are missing the boat when it comes to the

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.770
immediate and proximate causes of the insurrection
and of the coup attempt.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:31.080
And specifically, I'm talking about claims
that ultimately what happened last week comes

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:38.690
down to merely economic unfairness and inequality
and anger by the so-called working class.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:44.860
And even lots of people that I greatly respect
have weighed in on this issue, and I believe

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.860
they are wrong.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:51.270
I'll give you an example with total peace
and love, my former economics professor from

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:57.050
the University of Massachusetts, economist
Richard Wolffe, tweeted, quote, What was seen

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:02.920
in the Capitol building of Washington on January
six was another manifestation of angry working

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.440
class people.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.420
This will only continue unless basic changes
happen in this country.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.829
We need to do something about the inequality
of this society.

00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:14.020
I love Richard Wolffe.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.939
He's been a guest on this show a dozen times.

00:01:15.939 --> 00:01:18.060
I was recently on his show.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.920
This is the worst take I've ever seen from
Richard Wolffe, who typically has really great

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.659
takes to some degree.

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:29.650
This idea is a version of class reductionism.

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:36.780
Class reductionism is the idea that in the
end, all oppression, strife, violence, unrest,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:43.719
it all comes down merely to class struggle
and racial struggle is really class struggle

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:47.210
and nationalistic struggle is really class
struggle, etc.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.350
It's a gender struggle is really class struggle,
and that if we reduce inequality, it's going

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.469
to solve all of these different problems.

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:59.799
And I think we have to be very careful because
nobody's claiming that economics and class

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:07.180
struggle are not important in in just about
everything that we see in our political system.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:12.890
And even those claiming that it played a role
last week are right, but in this particular

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:20.060
case, the class struggle aspect of this, absent
a more detailed and comprehensive analysis,

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:23.750
falls woefully short in explaining what happened
last week.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:29.110
Remember shortly after Donald Trump was elected,
there was a whole bunch of talk about this

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:35.310
was about economic anxiety, economic anxiety,
motivated people to give Donald Trump a shot

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:38.620
because he spoke to those economic anxieties.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:45.260
And to some degree, it's true in that Donald
Trump as a faux populist, right wing populist,

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.480
that rhetoric certainly appeals to economic
anxiety in many people.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.620
But then as we had more information about
the motivations of Trump voters, we came to

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:01.010
learn that while there was economic anxiety
on both the left and the right, that the right

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:05.770
was motivated to vote for Donald Trump by
many other things, including the resonance

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:12.040
of Donald Trump's xenophobia, fear of losing
perceived or actual status to immigrants,

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.600
coming in and taking jobs to brown people,
asshole countries.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.090
That entire narrative.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:23.790
And case in point, there are so many counter
points to the class reductionist argument

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:30.780
or explanation about last week riots that
the explanation of this is merely class struggle

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:37.380
would be dangerous to accept as a full explanation
for what we saw, including, by the way, that

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.850
many of the people that participated in the
insurrection, they had the money to not only

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:45.030
travel to Washington, D.C., but to stay in
hotels that aren't cheap.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:49.880
Now, I know that there were groups funding
the travel, but for many people that wasn't

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:50.880
the case.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.650
These people were able to afford going to
D.C., taking time off from work if they have

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.460
a job, if they need to work and staying in
expensive hotels.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.330
And so there are.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.330
So that's one aspect.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:07.890
The other aspect is there are tons of people
on the left and right that economically are

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:11.860
way worse off than the protesters rioters
last week.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.710
But they were not there.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:18.349
And there are even examples of wealthy people
going to D.C. on private jets to participate

00:04:18.349 --> 00:04:20.259
in the riot, although that's anecdotal.

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:23.680
Obviously, most of these rioters did not fly
in on private jets.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:31.240
But the point here is that there is something
unique to those who, yes, mostly are not particularly

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:37.680
privileged economically, but there is a significant
xenophobic component.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:44.180
There is a significant ignorance to reality
component people who fall for, listen, if

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:50.360
this was just economic anxiety, you wouldn't
see that the people at the riot are the people

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:55.289
who fell for the obvious lies from Trump about
a stolen election.

00:04:55.289 --> 00:05:01.220
What was really the most common factor among
the rioters was that they fell for and they

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:06.610
believed that the election was stolen from
Donald Trump, which is demonstrably untrue.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.969
There were rich and poor people who fell for
that.

00:05:08.969 --> 00:05:13.060
There were elites and non elites who fell
for that, and importantly, poor people who

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.259
didn't fall for it.

00:05:14.259 --> 00:05:19.120
Weren't there rioting people who were significantly
more economically disadvantaged or oppressed

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.450
by the economic system? Weren't there rioting
because they didn't believe this stupid narrative

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:25.550
that the election was stolen?

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:32.430
And so I very much appreciate the class aspect
that at a general level has generated anxiety

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.409
and a desire for change.

00:05:34.409 --> 00:05:40.199
The people that participated in this riot
exposed the Trump movement for what it really

00:05:40.199 --> 00:05:41.199
is.

00:05:41.199 --> 00:05:43.620
And it's not merely an economic anxiety movement.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:50.310
It's a particularly extreme, radical, conspiratorial
worldview informed by being uninformed.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:55.259
That shirt, to some degree overlaps with aspects
of economic anxiety.

00:05:55.259 --> 00:05:59.710
But the truth is that at this point, economic
anxiety is a reality for a huge portion of

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:00.710
this country.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:05.400
That there I agree with Richard Wolffe and
others when half the country can't meet.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:11.449
An unexpected four hundred dollar expense
without going into debt, just about any group,

00:06:11.449 --> 00:06:17.080
unless you're saying we're only serving private
jet owners, just about any group, health care

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:22.139
workers, factory workers, educational workers,
whoever, all of these groups will include

00:06:22.139 --> 00:06:28.430
a lot of economic anxiety, but that doesn't
mean that that's the cause of violent, radical

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.559
insurrectionist violence.

00:06:30.559 --> 00:06:35.229
And let's not miss the forest for the trees
and pretend that it goes away simply by solving

00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:37.729
economic inequality.

00:06:37.729 --> 00:06:41.310
You listen, you'll solve economic inequality.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:46.590
And a lot of these people will be furious
that now they are on the same level as a lot

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.650
of people that they don't deserve.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:52.319
They don't believe, deserve believe to be
economically stable.

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:55.389
And that gets us back to the xenophobia and
the rest of it.

00:06:55.389 --> 00:06:58.449
So I think that these analyzes missed the
mark.

00:06:58.449 --> 00:07:01.960
I've seen a bunch of them, and I'm curious
to hear your thoughts.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:49.719
You can find me on Twitter 

00:07:49.719 --> 00:08:19.749
at 

00:08:19.749 --> 00:08:28.580
David Pakman,

